I figured I'd try a wishless ascension, seeing how previous ascensions 
had lines that said things like "you used 14 wishes." Depending on 
wishes, after a while, just seemed like a weakness in and of it's own.

I started out as a humble barbarian, hacking away at anything that would 
move with my axe (with the exception of my pet). My little dog was good 
at getting me into trouble, picking up a helm of opposite alignment 
(which I put right on my head, thus making me lawful instead of neutral).

I headed down and started with Sokoban. No problem, until I lost track 
of what I was doing and pushed a boulder right next to a door. I 
couldn't get past the boulder, so I decided to go to the gnomish mines 
to find a pick axe and remove the boulder.

I couldn't find a pick axe, but there was a lawfully aligned altar in 
minetown. I prayed at the altar, at which point Mistra was kind enough 
to remove the curse on the helm. I removed it and was restored to 
neutrality. I also found a cursed magic lamp in one of the stores, which 
I bought for the princely sum of 99 zorkmids (6 cha doesn't help). It 
proved to be a reliable light source the whole game, after I blessed it.

I eventually got a pick axe, went to the bottom of the mines, and got 
the luckstone. I then returned to Sokoban, removed the troublesome 
boulder, and found a bag of holding at the end. I got out of Sokoban and 
proceeded cautiously down.

I hit the jackpot on level 11. There were two altars on the level and a 
huge bones pile. The pile contained +4 GDSM, a +2 shield of reflection, 
gauntlets of power, and speed boots. It even had 3 magic markers. 2 of 
the markers were bone dry, but the third had ink left. I converted one 
of the altars and got Cleaver, then set about creating some holy water 
(to bless the marker) and write some blessed id scrolls to get a full ID.

I wrote the stupid marker dry and never got a full id. Hmpf. But seeing 
the shield of reflection, I figured I could get Vorpal Blade later (or 
something even better) and use the shield at a later date and then use 
the amulet slot for an AoLS. I left the shield near the altar, along 
with some other loot. My AC went down to around -15.

I went down the stairs and found the big room. The monsters converged, 
and as it so happened one of them had a wand of sleep. I woke up near 
the stairs just in time to go back up. I took a guess that the amulet in 
the pile was an amulet of reflection and guessed right. I put it on and 
dusted off the hoard.

Medusa wasn't too hard as a result, and neither was the castle (I tried 
on uncursed rings I had found until I came across a ring of levitation). 
I sacked the castle (never bothered to clear the towers to get the WoW) 
and proceeded down to the valley. No problem there either.

After that I went back to the altar on lvl 11 and sacrificed more stuff 
to get another artifact weapon. I got Vorpal Blade, ditched Cleaver, 
enchanted VB to +5, and enchanted my armor with some scrolls I had found 
and blessed. I then went on the quest. Amon Thoth got decapitated after 
a few rounds and I collected every bit of loot I could find. Some of the 
loot included two blessed scrolls of identify - I discovered I had two 
wands of polymorph and a wand of death. I polypiled a bunch of stuff and 
came up with a magic marker with 70 charges. I brought my armor up to 
snuff and charged a ring of protection to +5. That brought my AC down to 
-49.

I went down, killed off Rodney, and grabbed the AoLS in the tower (and 
the amulet of strangulation, too - I had plans for it). I went back to 
the altar with all the items I had found in hell so far and polypiled 
again, hoping to turn some of the worthless amulets and loot into good 
stuff. Despite several attempts, I didn't get any more AoLS, or even 
magic markers. But I did get a bunch of ID scrolls, which came in handy, 
and a LOT of magic mapping scrolls, which also came in handy. I also got 
another WoD, and a ring of conflict.

I went back to minetown, got some candles, and prepared to face Orcus. I 
wound up tunnelling underneath Orcus Town and using one of the bazillion 
create monster wands I had found until I produced a cockatrice. I used 
it to stone Orcus in one round - he never even got a chance to attack. I 
took his fully charged WoD (after smashing his statue) and chortled.

No major problem find the vibrating square, and no real problem killing 
Rodney. In fact, I only had to kill him four times, although he did 
manage to curse a lot of stuff. I had plenty of holy water prepared, though.

No problem killing the high priest. I grabbed the amulet and used 
confusion/gold detection spells to navigate the planes. The altar was 
the 2nd one I tried, although with -51 AC and 5 potions of full healing 
(and plenty of wands of teleportation I had saved up) the astral plane 
was more a nuisance than anything. Conflict certainly helps, and I 
contend that killing the angels your diety sends to punish you for 
wearing a ring of conflict at the end is well worth it.

All in all, the rng smiled on me for once. I can assume the Nethack Gods 
will punish me for my temerity of having such a lucky game in the 
future, but I have my barbarian ascension and my wishless conduct in 
hand. Between the bones find, polypiling like there was no tomorrow to 
get the stuff I needed and genociding 17 species, it wasn't terribly 
difficult.

Interestingly, however, I never did get the sleepless intrinsic. I 
looked for orange dragons, prayed like mad to get crowned (Crom ignored 
me except to note that he was well-pleased) but up until the end a sleep 
trap or potion of sleep would have me counting sheep. Luckily, it didn't 
prove fatal.

Oh, yeah - for the sake of the ongoing argument on the E word, I still 
didn't engrave it anywhere, and I used no wishes to accomplish my YAAP - 
just luck and technique.

Time to celebrate!


